WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:03.030
- All right, everybody,
let's close out the show

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:04.770
with something cool I
found on social media.

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:05.805
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:08.820
(rock music)

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.130
My kids are really into Legos.

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:12.120
I am as well.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.430
I kind of in fact pretend that it's them.

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:16.680
And it's me too, 'cause I
love putting them together.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.090
It's very therapeutic.

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:21.330
In fact, many people of all
ages are really into Legos.

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:24.000
But I've never seen anything
quite as elaborate as this.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.100
This is a love y'all.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.720
An Austin woman and her husband

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.270
have created a huge Lego
city in their house.

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:33.090
It's got pretty much everything
you can imagine and more.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:35.640
A thriving downtown, a fire station,

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:38.280
a residential neighborhood,
even a dog park.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:39.990
And as her TikTok followers know,

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:42.390
she never misses a single detail.

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:44.610
- [Emily] If you looked at a
downtown area of the Lego city,

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:45.780
this is where all my buildings are.

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.940
All my cars, Mystery Machine.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:50.370
Up here, this is like
our shopping district.

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:53.700
And we have a dog walker
actually with a few dogs.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:55.980
And what is that there?

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:56.820
Dog poop.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:57.653
Gross.

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:01.500
- We have her on the line
right now to tell us more.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:05.240
Everybody say hello to
Emily watching on KEYE TV.

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:06.917
What's up, Emily?

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:09.307
- Hello everyone.

00:01:10.323 --> 00:01:11.670
Wow, this is amazing.

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:12.810
- I'm gonna be honest with you,

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:14.820
I have tried to create
something cool like this

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:16.680
with my son in my house,

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.930
but nothing came close
to what you are doing.

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:19.800
It's incredible.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:22.410
So you have followers who
try to stump you, right?

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:24.300
With details on your Lego City.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:26.280
- Yeah, so a couple
weeks before that video

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:27.120
you all just watched,

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.800
some of my followers
were sending me questions

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:31.320
about my city like if I had random pieces.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:32.153
Do I have a pig?

00:01:32.153 --> 00:01:33.450
Do I have dog poop?

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:35.400
And so, I started
answering their questions

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:36.930
and pointing out what I have.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:40.410
And really I do have
pretty much everything.

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:41.760
My favorite part about the city though

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:44.850
has gotta be the natural area
with the working waterfall.

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:46.350
Me and my husband designed it on our own.

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:47.490
So there were no instructions.

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:49.050
It wasn't from an official set.

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:50.340
- Oh, I love that.

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:52.980
Man, Lego should call you for ideas.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:55.410
This is, that waterfall is rad.

00:01:55.410 --> 00:01:57.630
I saw it online how it
works and you twist.

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:58.560
It's very cool.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.120
How did you get into this?

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:03.270
- Yeah, so I feel like I'm one
of the few people out there

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:04.950
that never had Lego growing up.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:06.300
But when I met my husband,

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:07.920
he was really into Lego Star Wars sets.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:09.990
So we built a few of them together

00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:11.370
and then he got me my own set,

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:12.780
it's called the Women of NASA.

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:13.980
And it came with all these different

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:16.260
female mini figure scientists.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:17.490
I was actually getting my master's

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:18.540
in data science at that point,

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:19.980
so it really resonated with me.

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:21.600
And then after that I was really hooked.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:22.980
I love Lego Scooby-Doo.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:25.170
Like you can see a Mystery
Machine behind me here.

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:26.003
- Yes.

00:02:26.003 --> 00:02:29.100
- And you know, I started
posting Lego content

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:31.260
right after I lost my job during COVID,

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:32.610
which kind of bummed me out.

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:34.140
But I'm grateful for where it's come.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:35.640
And now I'm a Lego ambassador

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:38.040
and the Lego Ambassador
program's always really

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:40.530
looking for people to represent
different communities.

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:43.466
And I'm just so proud that I'm able

00:02:43.466 --> 00:02:45.960
to represent women who are
really just new fans of Lego.

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:47.190
It's so exciting.

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:49.590
- I am one of these women.

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:52.590
I literally will sit with my son.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:54.000
He will walk away and come back

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:54.930
and walk away and come back

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:57.300
and Mama's still there
putting it together.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:59.430
It's so, the task, like,

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:01.470
especially if you have
a chaotic life going on,

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:04.410
it's a nice thing that's just
an easy instruction to follow.

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:06.450
You're just, it's a
nice therapeutic thing.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:07.920
I'm just saying for any mamas out there

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.120
looking for something to
do with a glass of wine.

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:12.000
Thank you so much, Emily.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.080
I love your city.

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:13.920
It's awesome.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:14.753
- Thank you.

00:03:14.753 --> 00:03:15.907
- I'm liking your post right now.

00:03:15.907 --> 00:03:18.392
(audience cheering)

00:03:18.392 --> 00:03:19.320
And that's not all.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:20.910
Our season long partner Pilot Pen,

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:22.890
makers of FriXion, the go-to erasable pen

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:24.000
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.520
want to celebrate those
creating fearlessly

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:27.450
just like you, ma'am.

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:29.400
So they're gonna give you $1,000.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:30.233
How's that sound?

00:03:30.233 --> 00:03:31.746
(audience cheering)

00:03:31.746 --> 00:03:33.265
- Oh my God.

00:03:33.265 --> 00:03:34.430
Thank you so much.

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:35.574
- [Kelly] Absolutely.

00:03:35.574 --> 00:03:36.407
- [Emily] I can't believe that.

00:03:36.407 --> 00:03:38.082
- Thank you so much, Emily.

00:03:38.082 --> 00:03:39.750
And thank you to all our guests this hour.

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:43.410
Kate Mara, Dr. Jane Goodall,
Ava Louise Murchison

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:44.243
and Sydney.

00:03:44.243 --> 00:03:45.076
Y'all have a great day,

00:03:45.076 --> 00:03:46.770
and if it's not, try and change it.

